cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the data it produces, please cite both the
  software (this deposit) and the paper it supports.
title: >-
  Code and data for "Fifth-Harmonic Feedback Controls the Existence of a
  Third-Harmonic Zero"
abstract: >-
  Harmonic-balance solver, continuation, Floquet stability, and time-domain
  cross-checks for an exact third-harmonic response zero in a damped nonlinear
  absorber, together with one driver per reported result, the extracted data,
  and the figures as placed in the manuscript and its Supplemental Material.
type: software
